notes.body:
For the heuristics checks, you need to have at least 5 bytes captured (to avoid triggering an exception when calling tvb_get_string_enc()). The 11 bytes check seems also useful, but should likely done on the reported length rather than the captured one. Should we do instead?
```
if (tvb_reported_length(tvb) < 11 || tvb_captured_length(tvb) < 5){
    return false;
}
```
